    {
      "@id": "https://marlonbarrios.github.io/hybrid-intelligences/ontology#buddhism",
      "@type": [
        "skos:Concept",
        "hi:NetworkNode"
      ],
      "skos:prefLabel": "Buddhism",
      "skos:definition": "Tradition of practice and philosophy centered on suffering, interdependence, impermanence, and liberation—mindfulness, emptiness (śūnyatā), and non-self (anattā) as frameworks for understanding cognition, ethics, and embodied experience; foundational for enactivism via phenomenology and contemplative science. Vipassana (insight) is a core method of this tradition: first-person training of attention that later informed Varela’s neurophenomenology.",
