    {
      "@id": "https://marlonbarrios.github.io/hybrid-intelligences/ontology#cameron",
      "@type": [
        "skos:Concept",
        "hi:NetworkNode"
      ],
      "skos:prefLabel": "Cameron Buckner",
      "skos:definition": "Thursday July 23 — AI, authorship, ethics, and law. Professor of philosophy at the University of Florida and Donald F. Cronin Chair in the Humanities; specializes in philosophy of mind, cognitive science, and artificial intelligence. Author of From Deep Learning to Rational Machines: What the History of Philosophy Can Teach Us about the Future of Artificial Intelligence (Oxford, 2023). Teaches ethics, data, and technology.",
